# Call-site ledger of prometheus-client at 9b6b971f903e7a08f88da5a95048b7a2a28f55a5.
# Judgements: prometheus-client.md. Rules: macro-benchmark/README.md.
default reject prometheus_client.metrics_core.Metric.__eq__: no operand of this comparison, `in` test or key lookup is a Metric; the package never compares Metric objects (only clients do, e.g. assertEqual in the tests), and Metric defines __eq__ without __hash__, so it is unhashable and never a dict key or set element; the operands here are strs, numbers, bools, tuples, lists, dicts, sets, collectors, Samples or None
default reject prometheus_client.samples.Timestamp.__eq__: no operand of this comparison, `in` test or key lookup is a Timestamp (Timestamp defines __eq__ without __hash__, so it is unhashable and never a dict key or set element); the operands here are strs, numbers, bools, tuples or dicts of strs, lists of floats or None; the sites that compare Timestamps or lists of Samples that can hold them accept the candidate explicitly
default reject prometheus_client.samples.Timestamp.__ne__: no operand of this `!=` is a Timestamp; the two sites of the OpenMetrics parser that compare sample timestamps accept the candidate explicitly
default reject prometheus_client.samples.Timestamp.__lt__: no operand of this ordering comparison or sort is a Timestamp; the one site that orders sample timestamps (openmetrics/parser.py:616) accepts the candidate explicitly
default reject prometheus_client.samples.Timestamp.__gt__: no operand of this ordering comparison or sort is a Timestamp; the one site that orders sample timestamps (openmetrics/parser.py:616) accepts the candidate explicitly
default reject prometheus_client.samples.Timestamp.__float__: the argument of float() here is a str, int, float or bytes, never a Timestamp; the one site that converts a sample timestamp (exposition.py:306) accepts the candidate explicitly
default reject prometheus_client.samples.Timestamp.__str__: no formatted or str()-converted value here is a Timestamp; the values are strs, numbers, bools, tuples, lists, dicts or sets of them, exceptions, or client objects (B5); the sites that format a sample or exemplar timestamp accept the candidate explicitly
default reject prometheus_client.samples.Timestamp.__repr__: no value whose repr is taken here is a Timestamp (nor a container or Sample holding one); the site that formats a Metric's samples (metrics_core.py:50) accepts the candidate explicitly
default reject prometheus_client.metrics_core.Metric.__repr__: no formatted value here is a Metric or a container of Metrics; the package never formats a Metric (exposition.py:350 and openmetrics/exposition.py:166 add the metric to exception.args without formatting it)
default reject prometheus_client.metrics.MetricWrapperBase.__str__: no formatted value here is a metric wrapper; the sites that format `self` of a metric wrapper accept the candidate explicitly
default reject prometheus_client.metrics.MetricWrapperBase.__repr__: no value whose repr is taken here is a metric wrapper; the sites that format `self` with %r accept the candidate explicitly
default reject prometheus_client.django.exposition.PrometheusDjangoView.get: the receiver of this .get() is a dict, an os.environ mapping, a WSGI environ, the headers of a request, an ASGI scope or payload, or a ValueClass instance; the package never makes a PrometheusDjangoView (Django's view dispatch, a client, calls its get)
